  <article class="study"><a class="back" href="/#work">← Back to the work</a><header><p class="eyebrow">CASE STUDY 02 · EVENT BUSINESS GROWTH</p><h1>One operating picture for <i>revenue and growth.</i></h1><p>How HoneyBook, Sheets, Google Ads, Search Console, and manual follow-up became a secure action layer for Southern Revelry.</p></header><img class="study-hero lime-frame" src="/images/southern-dashboard.png" alt="Southern Revelry command center"/><div class="study-body"><aside><span>CLIENT</span><b>Southern Revelry</b><span>MARKETS</span><b>Austin + San Antonio</b><span>MY ROLE</span><b>Strategy, data, UX, engineering</b></aside><div><h2>The data existed. The story didn’t.</h2><p>HoneyBook managed client projects and payments. Sheets held years of leads. Ads generated demand. Search Console showed organic visibility. The owner still had to assemble the business story by hand.</p><blockquote>The command center turns existing systems into priorities, attribution, and action.</blockquote><h2>What changed</h2><ol><li>Every lead has one clear next step</li><li>Historical data stays traceable to its source</li><li>Ambiguous values get human review</li><li>Ads are measured against business outcomes</li><li>Organic search becomes an opportunity list</li><li>Integration health is visible, not assumed</li></ol><h2>Built safely, in useful phases</h2><p>The foundation delivered value before every external authorization was complete. Read-only connections came first; higher-risk advertising writes remained behind explicit approval gates.</p></div></div><div class="study-gallery"><img src="/images/southern-pipeline.png" alt="Southern Revelry sales pipeline"/><img src="/images/southern-seo.png" alt="Southern Revelry search opportunity dashboard"/></div><a class="next-study" href="/#contact">Talk about your operation <span>↗</span></a></article>
